<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Licinius Crassus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 115–53 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Crassus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> Crassus was a wealthy Roman politician and general, a member of the First Triumvirate with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. He invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> and was decisively defeated and killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Battle of Carrhae</a> in 53 BCE. The defeat showed the effectiveness of Parthian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a> against Roman legions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus.jpg" alt="Marcus Licinius Crassus" width="274" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Sosnovskiy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_a_Roman,_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
